+dnl medusa drives its worker threads through a cooperative shutdown path
+dnl (thr_pool_destroy() sets POOL_DESTROY and broadcasts pool_workcv, and the
+dnl workers leave their loop there).  pthread cancellation is only an
+dnl additional fast path, and not every libc provides it - musl, for instance,
+dnl does not implement pthread_cancel()/pthread_setcancelstate()/
+dnl pthread_setcanceltype() at all.  The functions are therefore probed and the
+dnl cancellation calls are compiled in only when they exist.
+AC_CHECK_FUNCS([pthread_cancel])
+
 CPPFLAGS="$CPPFLAGS -fPIC"
 CPPFLAGS="$CPPFLAGS -I/usr/include -I/usr/local/include -I${postgresql_prefix}/include/postgresql -I${postgresql_prefix}/include/pgsql -I${afpfsng_prefix}/include/afpfs-ng"
 
